/E (How will this affect their current foundational reading skills abilities? While screening for foundational reading skills is important and informative for making instructional decisions in early Kindergarten, students should experience substantial, consistent, systematic, structured instruction in foundational reading skills prior to considering a low reading score as a risk factor for dyslexia. Educators should allot time and provide materials from a high-quality curriculum for students to practice the foundational reading skills that follows a scope and sequence prior to considering a low reading score as a risk factor for dyslexia in Kindergarten.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
