/P 2054 0 R
/E (Some students over-rely on background knowledge, constructing explanations that seem plausible but are not grounded in what the text says. They answer from general world knowledge rather than from the passage itself.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
978 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2055 0 R
/E (Other students focus on surface-level details, identifying something true from the text without connecting it to the specific question being asked. They access textual information but do not integrate it into a coherent explanation.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
979 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2056 0 R
/E (Understanding causal and motivational relationships is particularly demanding, because these connections are rarely spelled out explicitly. Readers must infer why a character acted a certain way or how one event led to another.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
